WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.124 --> 00:00:02.669
- [Woman] How do you 
approach a challenge?

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.300
- I like challenges.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.507
One of the reasons I love being
a Jets fan is that they lose.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:11.984
A lot and I'm much 
more into the journey.

00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:16.088
I look at challenges as 
the narratives of my career.

00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:18.556
Whether this is 
egotistical or a nice thing,

00:00:18.556 --> 00:00:19.925
I'm not quite sure but

00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:23.460
I do think of things 
in the body of my work.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.792
The book will be very 
boring if everything's easy.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.094
You know, you need the arc and

00:00:27.094 --> 00:00:29.196
so when I see challenges,

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:31.798
I don't think that you 
get to have the luxuries

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.334
that come along with being 
a leader or CEO or a founder.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.904
If I want this, 
if I want the attention,

00:00:36.904 --> 00:00:40.073
if I want the fruits of the 
things that come along with it,

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.543
I have to be respectful that 
challenges come along with it

00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:45.279
so when they come to me

00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:46.246
I really kind of,

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.447
I'll paint you a picture.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.883
I genuinely love 
the scene in the movie,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.451
the cliche scene where the

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:54.054
person gets 
punched in the mouth,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.490
turns, blood comes out, 
spits out his tooth

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.393
and then looks back at the 
other person like, "Now, what?"

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:00.694
That's how I 
think about challenges.

00:01:00.694 --> 00:01:02.091
I weirdly want,

00:01:02.091 --> 00:01:03.537
I almost, can I get 
weird with you for a second?

00:01:03.537 --> 00:01:04.702
- [Woman] Yeah, you 
can get weird with me.

00:01:04.702 --> 00:01:08.101
- I even think sometimes 
I fabricate challenges

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:12.039
because I enjoy that 
more than the easy sailing.

00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:15.909
And so, I think any 
true purebred entrepreneur

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.078
has the stomach 
for challenges and

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.847
so for me it's just 
part of the equation.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:23.982
(light music)

